  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the task instructions and source-room tooling, then build the calculations, evidence register, workbook, report, presentation, and reproducibility checks. I’ll preserve the provided instruction files and record any data-quality limitations explicitly.",
    "I’m applying the installed OpenSocrates controller to the consequential recommendation: I’ll keep the evidence states, assumptions, uncertainty, and decision conditions explicit. I’m now collecting the frozen source-room index and its guidance before calculating anything.",
    "The source room is complete and contains synthetic client extracts plus archived official World Bank and ECB snapshots. The governing accounting rules are explicit: revision-winner reconciliation, order-level half-up rounding, sale-month FX, return quarantine, and scenario arithmetic with capex kept separate from annual contribution. I’m encoding those rules in one reproducible build script so every deliverable shares the same numbers.",
    "The first full build now succeeds. The independent verifier confirms the required JSON schema, monthly-to-country reconciliation, scenario constraints/payback convention, workbook tables, PDF text, and PPTX ZIP integrity. I’m doing the final packaging pass now, including a visual render check and a small audit of the recommendation’s stress-case alternative.",
    "The numbers are stable after adding explicit used/quarantined return sheets to the workbook. The base leader is CZE+ESP (EUR198,099 annual incremental contribution, EUR225,000 capex, 5 FTE, 1.14-year simple payback); POL+ESP is the strongest runner-up by base case, while the defined stress case ranks NLD+ESP highest. I’m preserving that distinction in the final caveats rather than collapsing it into one “certain” answer.",
